 "question": "E1 bounded every rule built on band-passed ZNCC at 31.2%. It did not bound a different similarity INPUT. driftforge/residual.py implements periodic cancellation and dense weighted ZNCC, but its own docstring records that it has only ever been used as a pool re-ranker -- 'the residual never relocates a candidate'. Does it discriminate when run densely as the PRIMARY matcher?",
