 "conclusion": "No difference. 36.7% vs 35.0%, paired McNemar 5 v 4, p=1.00. The true site is the global maximum in 14/60 under BOTH similarities. Periodic cancellation -- the mechanism at the heart of the Phase 1 method -- does not separate the true site from its lattice aliases when the reference and search are independent acquisitions, because the residual it recovers is dominated by uncorrelated acquisition noise rather than by shared aperiodic structure. Taken with E1, two independent similarity measures both handed the exact pose plateau at 31-37%, which closes the localization block on evidence.",
 "caveats": [
  "n=60; intervals are wide, but the conclusion needs only the upper bound to sit far below the ~100% that 40/40 requires.",
  "Arm B depends on estimate_lattice; low-confidence lattices were not excluded, so this is a fair end-to-end figure rather than a best-case one.",
  "p2_val only; no organizer data used."
